{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-surjective-morphism-implies-algebraic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{bootstrap-lemma-representable-by-spaces-over-space}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{criteria-lemma-algebraic-morphism-to-algebraic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d5e2b58c4032268dbed833bfc1b1836fb62b1b185d12e60410fb9cc821d5361d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ef59ecaf633439d25422293fb786ee5e42351f482713cb78c8976e6f363d4de", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAn application of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nis that something which is an algebraic space over an algebraic stack\nis an algebraic stack. This is the analogue of\nBootstrap, Lemma <REF_0002>.\nActually, it suffices to assume the morphism\n<MATH_0001> is ``algebraic'', as we will see in\nCriteria for Representability,\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9fd0efa7fa3aab5b392d9aac605304c98f31d92ff6efbdb7713423af7c8a59ac", "unit_id": "tag:04T0:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-representable-morphism-to-algebraic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:68d717bd988879712d4ba20a04c273b6df75460d6d0f1656c13c2f572892a4fc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3dc88a53d36a1906105c6badd1eb6e204f1f01f6098a5b13984000ffb9bba511", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a morphism of stacks in groupoids\nover <MATH_0004>. Assume that\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is representable by algebraic spaces, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> is an algebraic stack over <MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nThen <MATH_0008> is an algebraic stack over <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a2c6e9fa1cbaa8d0b9386618610051a48e8001b0746a37a042e1c87d19493358", "unit_id": "tag:05UM:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{V} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\mathcal{V} \\times_{\\mathcal Y} \\mathcal X$", "MATH_0006": "$1$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{U} \\to \\mathcal X$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-algebraic-stack}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-by-space-representable-by-space}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-representable-by-spaces}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-base-change-representable-transformations-property}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-surjective-morphism-implies-algebraic}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:102e20dda7b536c30d01fb58e5aea9874e779e28828c56811433a638fe9ef6b1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:330ceb5854a23498d135c798fc07e710707a95dd955c581b5e9f251f3e9e26e0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a surjective smooth <MATH_0002>-morphism\nfrom a representable stack in groupoids to <MATH_0003>. This exists by\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nThen the <MATH_0004>-fibre product\n<MATH_0005>\nis representable by an algebraic space by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe <MATH_0006>-morphism <MATH_0007> is representable by algebraic\nspaces, smooth, and surjective, see\nLemmas <REF_0003> and\n<REF_0004>.\nBy\nLemma <REF_0005>\nwe conclude that <MATH_0008> is an algebraic stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2c0c336c1cfb42ba2da3783d674ea57709cd09812405abce56e904f8680c34dc", "unit_id": "tag:05UM:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04T0", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\nRemoving the hypothesis that $j$ is a monomorphism was observed\nin an email from Matthew Emerton dates June 15, 2016\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$j : \\mathcal X \\to \\mathcal Y$", "MATH_0004": "$1$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$j$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-fibred-category-is-algebraic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b95fd9b5abbfa8b9e3073bbe33c73aa304d645c3b04a824fdad1420cdb76f7ac", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9774fe3aa1cd92d1f3194a8c699545dfeb426b6226286a42f9c62f5b564d7b0f", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme contained in <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a <MATH_0004>-morphism of\ncategories fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>.\nAssume <MATH_0006> is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThen, if <MATH_0007> is a stack in groupoids\n(resp.<SPACE_0001>an algebraic stack), so is <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ac375e5c46b68d8c941bd76658205b8477a00d94c25566911710df714e5cd3f", "unit_id": "tag:05UN:statement"}
